LZMA SDK decoder files (public domain) -- Igor Pavlov's C code for reading .7z archives.

Source:    https://github.com/ip7z/7zip  (a public mirror of the 7-Zip source releases)
Version:   7-Zip 26.06 sources (DOC/readme.txt "7-Zip 26.06 Sources"; 7zVersion.h MY_VERSION 26.06, 2026-11-06)
Commit:    d3296e39e1f1f92c7b41c0c3848e65640428d42d (2026-11-07)
Taken:     2026-11-24, by `git clone --depth 1`.
Directory: C/ of that tree.  The 7-Zip tree's C/ directory is the LZMA SDK's C code (the SDK is cut from it); the SDK's own
           statement, "LZMA SDK is written and placed in the public domain by Igor Pavlov" (DOC/lzma-sdk.txt of the SDK 18.05
           release, https://github.com/jljusten/LZMA-SDK, read for this check), is the licence the per-file headers repeat.
           The 26.06 files are used because they are the current release (18.05 is from 2018).

Licence:   every file here carries "Igor Pavlov : Public domain" in its first lines (7zVersion.h has the same words in its
           MY_COPYRIGHT_PD).  DOC/License.txt of the 7-Zip tree says: "Some files are 'public domain' files, if 'public domain'
           status is stated in source file", and that the other files are under the GNU LGPL; none of those is used here.
           No LGPL file, no RAR code, no encoder and no BSD file (ZstdDec.c, Xxh64.c) is part of this directory.

Files, copied unchanged (byte for byte; nothing was edited):
  7z.h 7zAlloc.c 7zAlloc.h 7zArcIn.c 7zBuf.c 7zBuf.h 7zCrc.c 7zCrc.h 7zCrcOpt.c 7zDec.c 7zStream.c
  7zTypes.h 7zVersion.h Bcj2.c Bcj2.h Bra.c Bra.h Bra86.c BraIA64.c Compiler.h CpuArch.c CpuArch.h Delta.c Delta.h
  Lzma2Dec.c Lzma2Dec.h LzmaDec.c LzmaDec.h Precomp.h RotateDefs.h

What is used: the 7z container reader (7zArcIn, 7zDec), LZMA and LZMA2 decoding (LzmaDec, Lzma2Dec), the branch filters (Bra,
  Bra86, BraIA64, Bcj2) and Delta, CRC-32 (7zCrc, 7zCrcOpt), the stream and allocation glue (7zStream, 7zAlloc, 7zBuf,
  CpuArch; the file stream itself is stdio, in sz_rom.c).  Not built in: PPMd (Z7_PPMD_SUPPORT is off, as in the SDK's default), AES, any encoder.
Used by: gpsp/vita/sz_rom.c (the app's .7z reader, own code, GPL-2.0-or-later like the app), built from gpsp/vita/app.mk.
  Only the main app links it; the SNES and Sega players are handed an unpacked file.

To verify: run `git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/ip7z/7zip` and compare each file with `cmp` against C/<file> at the commit above.
